:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="–"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>contain clusters of glycosphingolipids with longer-than-usual tails</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-285749" lvl="1" marL="557212" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="–"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>are more ordered </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-285749" lvl="1" marL="557212" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="–"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>contain specific doubly or triply acylated proteins</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-285749" lvl="1" marL="557212" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="–"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>allow segregation of proteins in the membrane</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="464" name="Google Shape;464;p63"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="762000"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="An image of membrane microdomains (rafts).&#xA;In the middle of the image are blue circles at the top and bottom; however, at the top, these blue circles become green and are much farther apart. Some blue circles are interspersed within the green circles. In the middle of the blue circles are the upside down and upright V-shaped tubes. Cholesterol is also represented in the middle with vertical peach tubes. Some of these attach to the green circles described above. To the bottom left, prenylated protein, shaped like a half-apple, breaks through the blue circles with black lines. In the middle left, at the bottom, red wavy lines represent acyl groups (palmitoyl, myristoyl). There is a purple tube that begins below the blue circles at the bottom and moves up vertically, then horizontally, then moves up and right, then down and right (in the middle of the top and bottom blue circles), then comes back down and goes horizontally along the blue circle line. It then comes down and circles around to the left. This is identified as caveolin. Just to the right of this, at the top, a GPI-linked protein, shaped like a half-apple, has a chain that goes to one pink circle between two green circles at the top. This pink circle has two red wavy lines going down. To the right of caveolin at the bottom, a doubly acylated protein, shaped like a half-apple, has two red wavy line coming up between the bottom blue circles. At the top is a bracket, labeled as raft, enriched in sphingolipids, cholesterol. This bracket spans from where the green circles described above begin to where they end." id="465" name="Google Shape;465;p63"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="4114800" y="1600200"/><a:ext cx="4878387" cy="3700462"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>